# Asgardeo JWT validation
# Derive from token endpoint: https://api.asgardeo.io/t/{org}/oauth2/token
AUTH_JWKS_ENDPOINT=
AUTH_ISSUER=
# Audience = your consumer key (client ID)
AUTH_AUDIENCE=
AUTH_TOKEN_VALIDATOR_ENABLED=
# Comma-separated corporate email domains, e.g. wso2.com,acquired-co.com.
# A logged-in caller whose email ends in one of these is treated as an
# internal employee with full access; anyone else is treated as an external
# auditor and confined to the audit-only routes (see internal/middleware
# callerGuard). Defaults to SCIM_USER_DOMAIN if left unset; if that's also
# unset, startup fails rather than silently locking out the whole company.
AUTH_INTERNAL_EMAIL_DOMAINS=
# Required (must be exactly "local") whenever AUTH_TOKEN_VALIDATOR_ENABLED=false.
# Disabling the validator skips signature verification AND turns every
# privilege check into allow-all, so config.Load() refuses to boot without
# this confirming the bypass is a developer's own machine. Leave unset in
# every deployed environment.
APP_ENV=

# Server. Bare port, no leading colon — matching .choreo/component.yaml's
# `port: 8081` and the Compliance Entity's SERVER_PORT. config.Load() adds the
# colon net.Listen needs; a legacy ":8081" is still accepted, so an environment
# that hasn't been updated keeps booting.
PORT=8081

# Compliance Entity (data layer + Azure file storage)
COMPLIANCE_ENTITY_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080

# HR entity GraphQL service (WSO2 employee lookup for Risk Identified By).
# Local: `go run ./cmd/hrmock`.
HR_ENTITY_GRAPHQL_URL=
HR_ENTITY_CLIENT_ID=
HR_ENTITY_CLIENT_SECRET=
HR_ENTITY_TOKEN_URL=

# Asgardeo SCIM2 — this platform's identity directory. Calls Asgardeo's own
# SCIM2 API directly (no digiops-infra SCIM Operations Service hop). The
# running server reads this via
# internal/config.SCIMConfig, to resolve a person's uuid to their name and
# email (see internal/directory and resolve.go) — required now that emails and
# display names are no longer stored in this database. cmd/backfill-uuids and
# the other backfill-* tools read the same var names directly for their own,
# offline use.
#
# Internal users and external auditors are genuinely separate Asgardeo
# organizations/app registrations — BASE_URL is the shared Asgardeo API root;
# everything else below is per-org. Only internal_user_mgt_view and
# internal_user_mgt_list are needed — this client only ever searches users.
SCIM_BASE_URL=https://api.asgardeo.io

# Each org's OAuth2 token endpoint is DERIVED, not configured:
# {SCIM_BASE_URL}/t/{SCIM_*_ORG}/oauth2/token — see internal/config.SCIMTokenURL,
# which the cmd/backfill-* tools call too so they authenticate against the same
# tenant the server does. SCIM_INTERNAL_TOKEN_URL and SCIM_EXTERNAL_TOKEN_URL
# are GONE: they were hand-written per environment and had to be kept in step
# with their org by hand, and a mismatch authenticated against the wrong tenant.
# Remove them from any environment that still sets them; they are ignored.
SCIM_INTERNAL_ORG=wso2
SCIM_INTERNAL_CLIENT_ID=
SCIM_INTERNAL_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Quoted: `source .env` runs this file as shell, and an unquoted space here
# parses as "assign SCIM_INTERNAL_SCOPES=internal_user_mgt_view, then run a
# command named internal_user_mgt_list" — silently NOT setting the full value.
SCIM_INTERNAL_SCOPES="internal_user_mgt_view internal_user_mgt_list"

SCIM_EXTERNAL_ORG=wso2external
SCIM_EXTERNAL_CLIENT_ID=
SCIM_EXTERNAL_CLIENT_SECRET=
SCIM_EXTERNAL_SCOPES="internal_user_mgt_view internal_user_mgt_list"

# RISK_MANAGEMENT_GROUP / RISK_OWNER_GROUP / RISK_COMPLIANCE_ADMIN_GROUP are
# GONE. The Management Approver and Risk Owner pickers used to filter
# Asgardeo group membership over SCIM; they now read user_role_grant directly
# (GET /grants/candidates), the same table their approval actions check — so
# a picked candidate can no longer lack the grant and 403 on first use.
# notifyComplianceAdmins (risk/handler/notify.go) resolves the Compliance
# Admin email notification the same way — GET /grants/candidates for
# RISK_COMPLIANCE_APPROVE — rather than a group, for the same reason. Remove
# these three vars from any environment that still sets them — they are
# ignored.

# AZURE_STORAGE_ACCOUNT_NAME / AZURE_STORAGE_ACCOUNT_KEY /
# AZURE_STORAGE_CONTAINER are NOT read here and never have been — this service
# has no Azure SDK dependency at all. File bytes go through the Compliance
# Entity, which holds the account key (see cmd/server/main.go's "the backend
# never talks to Azure directly"). Remove them from any environment that still
# sets them: an unused copy of a storage-account key is a credential to steal,
# not a config value. CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGIN is likewise ignored — the CORS origin
# is FRONTEND_BASE_URL (see below).

# Email notifications (email-service: POST /send-email). The service's own
# code has no auth check, but the real Choreo-hosted instance sits behind API
# Manager with OAuth2 client-credentials — same pattern as HR_ENTITY_* above.
EMAIL_SERVICE_URL=
EMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS=
EMAIL_CLIENT_ID=
EMAIL_CLIENT_SECRET=
EMAIL_TOKEN_URL=
# Master switch for ALL email from both modules. Only "true" / "false" are
# honoured; unset or any other value keeps the built-in default (on). Set to
# exactly "false" to make every send a no-op — emailer.Client short-circuits
# before any token fetch or HTTP call, so no risk or audit notification goes
# out. When "false", the five EMAIL_* vars above are also relaxed from required
# to optional, so a local/CI run needs no email credentials at all.
EMAIL_NOTIFICATIONS_ENABLED=
# Emails to a person's "lead" (their HR line manager, from the HR entity's
# managerEmail): the audit overdue-item digest to an owner's lead, and the risk
# escalation notice to the Risk Assigner's / Action Owner's leads. One switch
# for both modules — replaces the removed AUDIT_LEAD_ESCALATION_ENABLED. Only
# "true" / "false" honoured; unset/other keeps the built-in default (OFF, so
# current behaviour is unchanged). Risk still RESOLVES and freezes the leads on
# every escalation when this is off — the escalation-comment gate and the
# visibility carve-out need them — it just does not email them.
LEAD_ESCALATION_EMAILS_ENABLED=
# AUDIT_LEAD_ESCALATION_ENABLED is GONE — replaced by LEAD_ESCALATION_EMAILS_ENABLED
# above, which governs both modules. Remove it from any environment that still
# sets it; it is ignored.
# Public URL of the webapp — used to build the risk-detail link in emails,
# and as the CORS-allowed origin (there is no separate CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGIN
# var: both are the same "webapp's public origin", and having two meant one
# could be set correctly while the other silently defaulted elsewhere).
# Required regardless of EMAIL_NOTIFICATIONS_ENABLED (it is also the CORS origin).
FRONTEND_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Background scheduler (internal/scheduler). One switch for every daily sweep
# at once — the overdue-risk escalation and the audit due-date reminder digest,
# both fired at 08:00 UTC. Only "true" / "false" are honoured; unset or any
# other value keeps the built-in default (on). Set to "false" to stop both
# sweeps in an environment; the manual triggers
# (POST /api/v1/risks/escalations/run, POST /api/v1/audits/reminders/run) still
# work either way.
SCHEDULER_ENABLED=
